April 30th, Vietnamese Reunification Day, holds profound significance for the Vietnamese people. This day symbolizes the aspirations for peace, independence, and unity. The victory of April 30th ended the domination of both new and old colonialism that had existed for centuries in the southern region. From this point, our country officially entered a new era of autonomy and development.

To commemorate the 50th anniversary of April 30, 1975 - April 30, 2025, and the 139th International Labor Day (May 1, 1886 - May 1, 2025), civil servants and government employees will have 5 consecutive days off, from Wednesday (April 30, 2025) through Sunday (May 4, 2025).

&#x1F396;&#xFE0F; On this historic day, we honor the sacrifices of our forefathers who fought for the reunification of our nation. May their legacy inspire us to build a prosperous and united Vietnam.&#xA0;

