In response to the challenge of coal dust pollution in Quang Ninh, Hai Long Steel Structure was entrusted by the project owner with the responsibility for the fabrication and erection of the &quot;Dust Barrier Fence for the Coal Storage Facility at Cluster 3, Lang Khanh Port.&quot;

With a total steel structure volume a coverage area exceeding 7,500 square meters, this project is on the scale of a massive &quot;steel shield.&quot; The fence stands at a height of 13 meters and is engineered with a spatial truss system utilizing steel tubular members.

To ensure the longevity and durability of this large-scale steel structure in a coastal environment, Hai Long Steel Structure implemented hot-dip galvanizing&#x2014;a technology widely regarded as the &quot;gold standard&quot; for steel structures exposed to harsh conditions.

This structural solution was selected following meticulous engineering calculations, enabling the fence to withstand strong coastal winds and ensuring the overall stability and safety of the installation.

The dust barrier project at Lang Khanh Port is not merely a conventional steel structure; it represents a comprehensive solution and underscores Hai Long&apos;s strong commitment to supporting industrial development while safeguarding the environment.

